# Applies reviewed dependency fixes to the checksum-pinned Hermes v2026.8.27
# source metadata and frozen lock before installation.
#
# Hermes 0.20.6 already carries the reviewed aiohttp, cryptography, Pillow,
# Starlette, Tornado, and python-multipart selections natively. The remaining
# delta floors two stacks. First, mcp's unpinned HTTP stack: upstream pins
# httpx2==2.7.0 in the dev, mcp, and computer-use extras, and httpx2 2.7.0 plus
# its exact httpcore2==2.7.0 transitive carry GHSA-7mj9-2mp8-4m2p (SOCKS TLS
# downgrade), GHSA-8xx6-hgc6-gc2m (unbounded decompression),
# GHSA-f2fp-rgf2-35cp (quadratic SSE buffering), GHSA-h4x7-gw46-3wm6
# (multipart header injection), and GHSA-pf96-p4fj-6566 (CL/TE smuggling).
# httpx2 2.12.0 is the lowest release that clears all five advisories and
# requires httpcore2==2.12.0, which clears the same SOCKS-TLS flaw in the
# transport layer. Second, the dingtalk extra still pins
# alibabacloud-dingtalk==2.2.42; floor it at the reviewed 2.2.54 release (the
# selection recorded in the Hermes 0.19.0 dependency review) so the frozen lock
# cannot resolve the older build.
